# Search Area & Direction Area Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Add two mutually exclusive preview-mode features — Search Area (area autocomplete + map focus) and Direction Area (wall-aware A* routing between a From origin and a To destination) — to `PreviewOverlay.tsx`.

**Architecture:** Feature-toggle state (`"search" | "direction" | null`) lives in `PreviewOverlay`. A shared `AreaAutocomplete` component powers area search in both features. A pure `pathfinder.ts` module rasterizes walls onto a grid and runs A* in canvas pixel space; the result is converted to lng/lat and rendered as a MapLibre GeoJSON LineString layer. Single-level enforcement is computed from existing `visibleLevelIds` + `canvasData.levels` — no store changes needed.

**Tech Stack:** TypeScript 5, React 19, MapLibre 5, Zustand 5, Next.js 16, Tailwind 4, lucide-react

## Global Constraints

- Do not add any new npm dependencies
- Do not modify `useMapStore.ts` — no new state fields or actions
- All TypeScript must pass `npx tsc --noEmit` with zero new errors
- ESLint must pass with `npx eslint src/ --ext .tsx,.ts`
- CSS uses only existing CSS variables: `var(--editor-canvas-white)`, `var(--editor-rich-black)`, `var(--editor-subtle-ash)`, `var(--editor-midtone-gray)`, `var(--editor-ghost-gray)`, `var(--editor-shadow-card)`, `var(--editor-shadow-popover)`
- Commit after every task

