            background: "#eff6ff",
            borderColor: "#bfdbfe",
            color: "#1d4ed8",
          }}
          title="Set as Direction To destination"
        >
          <Navigation className="size-3" /> Directions
        </button>
      )}
      <button onClick={() => setSelection(null)} className="flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-[8px] hover:bg-(--editor-ghost-gray)">
        <X className="size-4" style={{ color: "var(--editor-midtone-gray)" }} />
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  ```

- [ ] **Step 12: Run typecheck and ESLint**

  ```bash
  npx tsc --noEmit
  npx eslint src/components/editor/PreviewOverlay.tsx src/components/editor/preview --ext .tsx,.ts
  ```
  Expected: zero errors

- [ ] **Step 13: Commit**

  ```bash
  git add src/components/editor/PreviewOverlay.tsx
  git commit -m "feat(preview): wire Search Area and Direction Area features into PreviewOverlay"
  ```

---

## Self-Review: Spec Coverage Check

| Spec requirement | Covered by |
|---|---|
| 1. Mutually exclusive toggle | Task 5 Step 9: clicking active feature deactivates it |
| 2. Search Area — text input top-right with autocomplete | Task 3 + Task 5 Step 10 |
| 3. Search Area — only areas with info | `AreaAutocomplete.candidatesWithInfo` filters by `infoId` |
| 4. Search Area — pan + show info on select | Task 5 Step 8: `handleSearchSelect` calls `setSelection` |
| 5. Direction Area — From/To UI | Task 4 `DirectionPanel` |
| 6. Direction To — autocomplete (title + description) | `AreaAutocomplete` with `showDescription=true` |
| 7. Direction To — via "Direction" button in info card | Task 5 Step 11 |
| 8. Direction From — Select Area mode (title-only dropdown) | `AreaAutocomplete` with `showDescription=false` |
| 9. Direction From — Dropped Location mode | Task 5 Steps 6–7 |
| 10. Route Select Area — blue path between centroids | Task 5 Steps 3+5: `routePath` useMemo + route line layer |
| 11. Dot markers at area centroids (areas with info) | Task 5 Step 4: `preview-area-dots` circle layer |
| 12. Route Dropped Location — pin to centroid | `fromPin` used as from-point in `routePath` useMemo |
| 13. Wall-aware pathfinding / shortest path | Task 1: `buildGrid` + `findPath` |
| 14. "No route available" message | Task 4: DirectionPanel shows banner when `routeStatus === "none"` |
| 15. Single-level constraint — disabled/banner | Task 5 Step 10: `!isSingleLevel` guard on both panels |
| 16. Single-level — only active level areas in results | Task 5 Step 2: `activeAreas = singleLevel?.layout.areas` |

**Known limitation:** The dropped-pin inverse projection (Task 5 Step 7) uses a linear approximation. It is accurate for floor plans under 500 m span. If a future plan adds support for very large buildings, expose `lngLatToPixel` from `geojson-utils.ts`.
